WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.730
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:02.000 --> 00:05.580
<i>It all began, freshmen year of high school.</i>

3
00:08.560 --> 00:11.090
[Year 1, Class 2]

4
00:11.090 --> 00:14.610
You broke up with your girlfriend, Serizawa?

5
00:14.610 --> 00:16.810
Why? She seemed like a nice girl.

6
00:16.810 --> 00:19.450
She was, but...

7
00:19.450 --> 00:23.060
Same reason as always, huh?

8
00:23.060 --> 00:27.200
<i>I never really understood what it meant to romantically "like" someone.</i>

9
00:27.980 --> 00:29.650
Morning.

10
00:29.650 --> 00:30.920
Morning!

11
00:30.920 --> 00:33.370
<i>I liked chatting with people.</i>

12
00:33.370 --> 00:35.140
<i>And I liked that others liked me.</i>

13
00:35.140 --> 00:37.680
- I'm feeling eh. - Aw, too bad.

14
00:37.680 --> 00:40.000
- See you! - Later.

15
00:41.940 --> 00:43.570
<i>But...</i>

16
00:49.180 --> 00:53.010
<i>I never felt the desire</i>

17
00:54.850 --> 00:56.800
<i>to reach out to someone myself.</i>

18
00:57.850 --> 01:00.900
[Indoor voices - Library Committee]

19
01:04.560 --> 01:06.800
Long story short,

20
01:06.800 --> 01:11.000
your indifference made the girl anxious,

21
01:11.000 --> 01:15.590
and before you knew it, she self-destructed.

22
01:16.980 --> 01:21.630
I'm seriously the worst.

23
01:21.630 --> 01:23.500
Don't blame yourself too hard.

24
01:23.500 --> 01:27.090
You can't choose who you love.

25
01:27.910 --> 01:30.540
I know that, but still...

26
01:30.540 --> 01:32.300
If you're going to mope,

27
01:33.010 --> 01:34.730
do your job.

28
01:34.730 --> 01:36.940
[Returns] [Borrowing]

29
01:36.940 --> 01:38.840
Yes, sir.

30
02:07.280 --> 02:11.710
<i>That was when I met him.</i>

31
02:50.480 --> 02:56.270
<i>A boy I didn't know was engrossed in a book.</i>

32
02:56.270 --> 02:59.800
<i>That's all it was.</i>

33
03:11.610 --> 03:15.660
<i>But for some reason, I couldn't take my eyes off of him.</i>

34
03:24.670 --> 03:27.080
<i>My heart was set ablaze.</i>

35
03:27.080 --> 03:31.230
<i>It was an emotion I'd never experienced before.</i>

36
04:15.360 --> 04:18.750
[Episode 7]

37
04:18.750 --> 04:20.500
Great timing, Serizawa.

38
04:20.500 --> 04:23.250
- Could you handle those... - Yes, sir!

39
04:30.610 --> 04:35.800
<i>My interest for him grew by the day.</i>

40
04:37.420 --> 04:39.920
Rock paper scissors, shoot!

41
04:39.920 --> 04:42.150
And shoot!

42
04:42.150 --> 04:44.060
Look over there!

43
04:44.060 --> 04:45.870
- Score! - Aw, man.

44
04:45.870 --> 04:48.150
Let's just call it your win.

45
04:48.150 --> 04:51.030
Serizawa, you're helping at the library again?

46
04:51.030 --> 04:54.310
- Yeah. - Seriously? Any reason why?

47
04:54.310 --> 04:57.090
Well, you know.

48
04:57.090 --> 04:58.580
Huh?

49
05:20.710 --> 05:23.010
Suzuki. Let's head home together.

50
05:23.010 --> 05:24.450
Yeah.

51
05:24.450 --> 05:25.890
I'm beat.

52
05:25.890 --> 05:28.190
Same.

53
05:30.910 --> 05:33.480
So, his name is Suzuki.

54
05:35.470 --> 05:39.130
Suzuki, Suzuki... [Returns]

55
05:41.040 --> 05:43.810
Huh? He's not listed.

56
05:43.810 --> 05:46.260
He doesn't borrow out any books?

57
05:48.090 --> 05:52.890
Then what is he always so excited to read?

58
06:07.520 --> 06:08.810
What're you looking at?

59
06:08.810 --> 06:10.220
Nothing.

60
06:10.220 --> 06:12.800
I'm just glad you're motivated.

61
06:47.110 --> 06:49.380
What is he reading?

62
07:18.220 --> 07:19.800
I'm yakisoba bread, all the way.

63
07:19.800 --> 07:21.680
Really?

64
07:21.680 --> 07:23.730
Red bean bread is great, too.

65
07:23.730 --> 07:26.110
What is he reading?

66
07:31.640 --> 07:36.790
<i>If it were anyone else, I could just ask. But not Suzuki.</i>

67
07:49.330 --> 07:51.630
What is he reading?

68
08:06.120 --> 08:07.930
What's he up to?

69
08:10.280 --> 08:11.840
Join the judo team.

70
08:11.840 --> 08:13.010
Why?

71
08:13.010 --> 08:16.290
To make the most of our youth!

72
08:16.290 --> 08:18.280
Want me to sign up?

73
08:18.280 --> 08:20.450
- For real? - You're serious?

74
08:20.450 --> 08:22.060
Just kidding.

75
08:22.060 --> 08:23.440
- And you? - I'll throw you.

76
08:23.440 --> 08:25.180
Amateur.

77
08:25.180 --> 08:26.720
Yeah?

78
08:30.500 --> 08:33.230
Serizawa?

79
08:33.230 --> 08:34.410
Hello?

80
08:34.410 --> 08:37.790
Earth to Serizawa?

81
08:38.780 --> 08:41.340
- Maybe he's serious now. - You think?

82
08:41.340 --> 08:43.180
Wait, he turned in.

83
09:04.480 --> 09:07.360
- I'll take this. - Thank you.

84
09:16.780 --> 09:20.500
[Tatakiwari Ishibashi's works]

85
09:20.500 --> 09:24.160
[Moon in the Deep Sea]

86
09:26.880 --> 09:28.640
BL?

87
09:29.800 --> 09:34.230
[Moon in the Deep Sea]

88
09:34.230 --> 09:36.060
<i>I want you to look at me.</i>

89
09:36.060 --> 09:39.680
<i>Our relationship will be changed forever.</i>

90
09:39.680 --> 09:42.020
<i>I want to really know you.</i>

91
09:42.020 --> 09:44.810
<i>If you get any closer, we can't go back.</i>

92
09:44.810 --> 09:47.060
<i>I don't want to.</i>

93
09:47.060 --> 09:50.870
<i>I'm fine with our relationship changing.</i>

94
09:50.870 --> 09:54.850
- <i>I can't hold back anymore.</i> - <i>Neither can I.</i>

95
09:56.420 --> 09:59.310
What the heck?

96
09:59.310 --> 10:02.150
This is so exhilarating.

97
10:03.910 --> 10:07.030
Huh? Hold on.

98
10:07.030 --> 10:11.340
Is this why Suzuki looked like that?

99
10:18.110 --> 10:21.180
Seriously?

100
10:21.180 --> 10:23.090
No way.

101
10:24.400 --> 10:27.080
That's so cute.

102
10:29.160 --> 10:31.110
<i>"Cute".</i>

103
10:32.120 --> 10:35.620
<i>Once I verbalized it, I couldn't stop myself.</i>

104
10:45.110 --> 10:46.900
Cute.

105
10:49.380 --> 10:51.740
Are you okay?

106
10:51.740 --> 10:53.770
Yeah. I just dropped the eraser.

107
10:53.770 --> 10:55.410
Let me help.

108
10:55.410 --> 10:57.340
Thanks.

109
10:57.340 --> 11:00.050
<i>I want to know more about him.</i>

110
11:04.320 --> 11:07.120
<i>I want to get closer to him.</i>

111
11:12.550 --> 11:14.600
Cute.

112
11:14.600 --> 11:17.770
Suzuki. You got some on your mouth.

113
11:19.250 --> 11:20.420
There.

114
11:20.420 --> 11:22.510
Thanks.

115
11:28.420 --> 11:30.000
<i>More.</i>

116
12:21.100 --> 12:25.220
<i>At some point, I had become</i>

117
12:25.220 --> 12:27.880
<i>hopelessly obsessed with Suzuki.</i>

118
12:31.420 --> 12:33.060
<i>And yet...</i>

119
12:41.420 --> 12:45.870
<i>I was afraid talking to him would scare him away.</i>

120
12:47.790 --> 12:50.220
Suzuki! Morning.

121
12:50.220 --> 12:51.510
- Morning. - Let's go.

122
12:51.510 --> 12:52.970
Yeah.

123
12:54.140 --> 12:56.630
You look tired. Up late doing homework?

124
12:56.630 --> 12:58.430
- We had homework? - Yeah.

125
12:58.430 --> 12:59.810
Really?

126
12:59.810 --> 13:05.650
<i>The days passed without ever reaching out to him.</i>

127
13:06.550 --> 13:09.800
<i>Near the end of freshman year...</i>

128
13:09.800 --> 13:11.200
I'm starving.

129
13:11.200 --> 13:12.970
- What're you getting? - Curry bread.

130
13:12.970 --> 13:14.990
- Again? - Seriously?

131
13:21.530 --> 13:26.480
<i>Suzuki began to spend more time alone.</i>

132
13:30.970 --> 13:32.150
Huh? BL?

133
13:32.150 --> 13:33.440
Like, boys' love?

134
13:33.440 --> 13:34.620
I get it now.

135
13:34.620 --> 13:37.580
Of course not. That's just gross.

136
13:40.540 --> 13:41.740
Did you do it?

137
13:41.740 --> 13:44.000
Did not!

138
13:44.000 --> 13:47.010
It's so awkward with Suzuki now.

139
13:47.010 --> 13:48.520
Yeah, seriously.

140
13:48.520 --> 13:50.500
He's always absorbed in his BL.

141
13:50.500 --> 13:51.670
And his face!

142
13:51.670 --> 13:54.420
- He gets so red! - Yeah, ew!

143
13:54.420 --> 13:56.330
You guys, knock it off.

144
13:56.330 --> 13:57.480
- What? - Why?

145
13:57.480 --> 13:59.970
You said it yourself that BL was gross.

146
13:59.970 --> 14:02.470
- Yeah, you agreed with us. - Well, I...

147
14:02.470 --> 14:04.900
Hey.

148
14:05.590 --> 14:08.690
I heard something about BL.

149
14:08.690 --> 14:11.000
Mind if I join in?

150
14:14.770 --> 14:18.300
I'm also a BL fan.

151
14:20.840 --> 14:23.140
- Let's go. - Yeah.

152
14:29.910 --> 14:32.250
Pathetic.

153
15:24.720 --> 15:27.280
<i>Suzuki.</i>

154
15:29.320 --> 15:33.010
<i>What did those guys say to you?</i>

155
15:35.590 --> 15:37.920
<i>Were you frustrated?</i>

156
15:37.920 --> 15:39.850
<i>Were you hurt?</i>

157
15:47.830 --> 15:52.180
<i>Frankly, I was pissed off.</i>

158
16:01.380 --> 16:04.510
<i>Not only at the people who hurt you,</i>

159
16:04.510 --> 16:09.760
<i>but at myself, for not being able</i>

160
16:09.760 --> 16:11.510
<i>to protect you.</i>

161
16:20.320 --> 16:22.290
What's up, Serizawa?

162
16:22.290 --> 16:24.200
I thought we had dinner plans today.

163
16:24.200 --> 16:25.560
Sorry.

164
16:25.560 --> 16:28.040
Could I ask you guys a question?

165
16:28.870 --> 16:33.860
If I said I liked BL, how would you all react?

166
16:33.860 --> 16:36.120
Huh? That's a random question.

167
16:36.120 --> 16:39.450
If you like BL, so what? We wouldn't care.

168
16:39.450 --> 16:40.790
Right?

169
16:40.790 --> 16:42.200
Yeah.

170
16:42.200 --> 16:44.870
More importantly, I'm starving.

171
16:44.870 --> 16:47.380
I knew it.

172
16:47.380 --> 16:52.870
People like you guys exist, so why do others have to hurt him?

173
16:55.810 --> 16:57.970
Something happened, didn't it?

174
16:57.970 --> 17:01.020
What's up? We'll listen.

175
17:01.020 --> 17:02.970
Here, have some chocolate.

176
17:02.970 --> 17:04.510
It'll help.

177
17:05.810 --> 17:07.280
Okay, I've decided.

178
17:07.280 --> 17:10.130
I'm going to become his friend.

179
17:10.130 --> 17:11.480
Huh?

180
17:11.480 --> 17:13.810
I won't scare him.

181
17:13.810 --> 17:17.110
I'll approach him slowly.

182
17:17.110 --> 17:23.480
And when I become his bestest friend, he can talk all about his hobby with me.

183
17:23.480 --> 17:25.840
What's he going on about?

184
17:25.840 --> 17:30.470
But first things first, I need to brush up on my BL.

185
17:30.470 --> 17:32.960
Dude, you good?

186
17:33.810 --> 17:37.720
I'm going to become the King of BL!

187
17:40.760 --> 17:42.600
What?

188
17:43.740 --> 17:47.210
<i>Sophomore year began.</i>

189
17:50.510 --> 17:53.830
Please put us in the same class.

190
17:54.900 --> 17:56.980
I'll be back soon.

191
18:06.960 --> 18:09.590
I'm with you chumps, again?

192
18:09.590 --> 18:11.000
Aw, come on. [Year 2, Class 1]

193
18:11.000 --> 18:12.170
We know you're happy!

194
18:12.170 --> 18:14.640
Am not.

195
18:22.220 --> 18:24.210
Score!

196
18:25.450 --> 18:30.450
<i>I sent a "thank you" to the BL gods.</i>

197
18:30.450 --> 18:33.440
[Hajime Suzuki]

198
18:55.840 --> 18:58.540
Suzuki, you dropped this.

199
18:58.540 --> 19:00.000
Here.

200
19:02.140 --> 19:04.140
Th-Thanks.

201
19:07.660 --> 19:09.810
<i>That being said...</i>

202
19:11.030 --> 19:12.990
Bowling or karaoke?

203
19:12.990 --> 19:15.480
- What's the move? - I say the gym!

204
19:15.480 --> 19:16.920
- Denied. - Overruled.

205
19:16.920 --> 19:19.620
- Not happening. - What about you, Serizawa?

206
19:19.620 --> 19:20.840
Hey, there's a party room available!

207
19:20.840 --> 19:22.840
Seriously?

208
19:22.840 --> 19:24.290
Do they have weights there?

209
19:24.290 --> 19:26.540
Y-Yeah. I think so.

210
19:26.540 --> 19:29.690
Hey, good for you, Iwasaki!

211
19:29.690 --> 19:31.480
Suzuki.

212
19:31.480 --> 19:33.750
We're going out as a class after this.

213
19:33.750 --> 19:36.280
Wanna join?

214
19:37.090 --> 19:38.740
Sorry.

215
19:38.740 --> 19:41.560
I'm not good with social events.

216
19:43.150 --> 19:46.130
No worries. Sorry to put you on the spot.

217
19:46.130 --> 19:48.180
Let's go again some other time.

218
19:56.500 --> 20:01.600
<i>I couldn't close the gap between us so easily.</i>

219
20:01.600 --> 20:05.130
[Idea Journal]

220
20:07.780 --> 20:09.970
A journal?

221
20:11.570 --> 20:14.950
<i>That day, I was given a miracle.</i>

222
20:19.010 --> 20:22.920
[Haruto Serizawa]

223
20:33.410 --> 20:36.030
You write about a "Haruto Serizawa" in here.

224
20:36.030 --> 20:37.470
Is that supposed to be me?

225
20:37.470 --> 20:38.670
<i>And then...</i>

226
20:38.670 --> 20:41.050
Give me the honor

227
20:41.050 --> 20:42.800
of being your first reader.

228
20:42.800 --> 20:47.820
<i>After discovering Suzuki's secret, I became his very first reader.</i>

229
20:48.690 --> 20:50.870
<i>Then, I became his friend.</i>

230
20:51.810 --> 20:53.730
<i>Eventually, we went on a date.</i>

231
20:55.270 --> 20:59.230
Suzuki. Look at me.

232
21:01.120 --> 21:03.030
<i>And finally, we kissed.</i>

233
21:04.810 --> 21:07.540
<i>Now, back to present day.</i>

234
21:08.260 --> 21:10.420
I'm sorry!

235
21:10.420 --> 21:14.090
I can't go on a date with you.

236
21:16.040 --> 21:19.510
Why not?

237
21:22.710 --> 21:24.520
I...

238
21:24.520 --> 21:28.880
<i>I already know</i>

239
21:29.820 --> 21:31.990
<i>what this feeling is.</i>

240
21:31.990 --> 21:34.950
I have someone I like.

241
21:44.710 --> 21:46.320
Suzuki.

242
21:47.660 --> 21:49.330
Serizawa.

243
21:51.450 --> 21:56.180
<i>When I call out to him, he greets me with a smile.</i>

244
21:57.710 --> 21:59.290
<i>But...</i>

245
22:00.710 --> 22:02.670
<i>That's still not enough.</i>

246
22:06.340 --> 22:08.340
What're you reading?

247
22:10.290 --> 22:12.890
A manga I bought yesterday.

248
22:12.890 --> 22:16.460
Look, isn't this bottom way too dense?

249
22:16.460 --> 22:18.770
Huh? Why?

250
22:18.770 --> 22:20.120
See, look.

251
22:20.120 --> 22:22.980
The top's clearly obsessed with him,

252
22:22.980 --> 22:25.000
but the bottom totally doesn't notice.

253
22:25.000 --> 22:26.650
You're right.

254
22:26.650 --> 22:28.660
That's cute.

255
22:35.070 --> 22:37.740
Hopefully, he catches on soon.

256
22:38.620 --> 22:43.400
<i>The first person I ever fell for.</i>

257
22:44.610 --> 22:46.630
Let's get going.

258
22:46.630 --> 22:48.520
No.

259
22:48.520 --> 22:50.320
- Serizawa? - No.

260
22:50.320 --> 22:51.650
No.

261
22:51.650 --> 22:52.890
No, no, no!

262
22:52.890 --> 22:54.730
We have to leave eventually.

263
22:54.730 --> 22:58.260
<i>I don't intend on letting him get away.</i>

264
22:58.260 --> 22:59.900
No.

265
22:59.900 --> 23:02.210
Let's make summer memories together, Suzuki.

266
23:02.210 --> 23:03.950
I do have someone I like.

267
23:03.950 --> 23:06.990
They're cute, kind, and hardworking.

268
23:06.990 --> 23:09.160
Know who I'm talking about?

269
23:09.160 --> 23:11.050
All right, ready?

270
23:11.050 --> 23:14.900
<i>There is someone who meets all those conditions.</i>
